// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6001 new: 13 Linux detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6001
// Pull request author: saakovv
// Change: new rule
// Title: Linux Dangerous Capability Set via Setcap
// Sigma ID: f3b8a4d2-5c9e-4f64-a2b3-4d1c6e9f8a30
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ivan Saakov
// Date: 2026-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1548.001
// Description: Detects use of setcap to assign dangerous Linux capabilities to an executable file. Capabilities
//   such as cap_setuid, cap_sys_admin, cap_sys_ptrace, cap_sys_module, and cap_net_raw enable
//   privilege escalation without a SUID bit, making them harder to detect. Attackers assign these
//   capabilities to binaries they control to maintain persistent elevated access or to facilitate
//   lateral movement by enabling low-privileged accounts to perform root-level operations.
// False positives:
//   - Package installation scripts that legitimately set capabilities on ping or similar utilities
//   - Container runtime configuration setting required capabilities
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/#capabilities
//   - https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/setcap.8.html
//   - https://linux.die.net/man/7/capabilities
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5bac28da3655c33390db7ef1503db8cd3babb5f/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_setcap_dangerous_capabilities.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/setcap" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_setuid" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_setgid" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_sys_admin" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_sys_module" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_sys_ptrace" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_sys_rawio" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_dac_override" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_dac_read_search" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_net_raw" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_net_admin" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_bpf" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_setpcap" or ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_mac_admin")) and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "cap_net_raw+ep /bin/ping"))
